{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "aim",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 🧭 What this vault is for\n\n**HRM / HRM-X** is a study of *understanding as operator inference*.\n\nA task is a **situation + operator + question**. Understanding means inferring the operator and executing it exactly, then checking the answer in a representation different from the one that produced it.\n\nSince v0.5 a hypothesis is not a program the mind searches for. It is a **family** — the exact solution set of a law set — fitted exactly over ℚ.\n\nWhat this project is **not**:\n- not a language model, and not a chain-of-thought prompt;\n- not a library lookup dressed up as reasoning;\n- not a model of perception (ADR-009 measured that as the broken component);\n- not a description of any large trained checkpoint.",
      "x": -1780,
      "y": -760,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 460,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "rules",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### 📐 How to read this canvas\n\nFour columns, left to right:\n\n1. **The model** — the code that runs today.\n2. **The baselines** — kept alive so every claim has something to be compared against.\n3. **The evidence** — the specs and ADRs that say what is claimed and what is refused.\n4. **The concepts** — background for our own design only.\n\nEverything in `External Research/` is deliberately *outside* this picture. See [[00 - Knowledge Graph Index]].",
      "x": -1780,
      "y": -260,
      "width": 460,
      "height": 340,
      "color": "1"
    },
